<%!-- [LEGAL REVIEW] Placeholder terms: Stage 10 finishes the legal pages.
     The "What you upload" section is what sign-up, guest uploads and
     music uploads ask people to agree to; keep its meaning when editing. --%>
<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_scope={@current_scope} shell={:plain}>
  <article
    id="terms"
    class="mx-auto flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-6 py-12 text-[15px] leading-relaxed"
  >
    <header class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="text-ks-muted">Version {@version}</p>
      <p
        id="terms-review-note"
        class="rounded-box border border-accent/40 bg-ks-amber-soft px-4 py-3 text-sm"
      >
        [LEGAL REVIEW] These terms are a working draft and will be reviewed before launch.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section id="terms-service" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">The service</h2>
      <p>
        Keepsake lets you make photo albums and share them with the people you choose,
        behind a link and a private code. By creating an account you agree to these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-uploads" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">What you upload</h2>
      <p>
        You keep ownership of the photos, music and words you add. You must own them, or
        have permission from whoever does, to upload and share them. That includes music
        you add to a slideshow: you are responsible for having the rights to use it, and
        for any claim that you didn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        Guests who add photos to an album confirm the same for the photos they add.
        The album's owner decides what is shown.
      </p>
      <p>
        You give us permission to store, resize and show your content only to run the
        service for you and the people you share with.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-removal" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Content we may remove</h2>
      <p>
        We may remove content, or pause an account, when we receive a credible report that
        it infringes someone's rights, breaks the law or harms others.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="terms-account" class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">Your account</h2>
      <p>
        Keep your password safe. You can export everything or delete your account at any
        time from Settings.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
